1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:03,680
I've been waking up, usually naturally, around 6 a.m.
最近我通常在早上六点左右自然醒。

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:07,190
Or if not, I'll have an alarm set for 6:15.
如果没自然醒，我也设了六点十五分的闹钟。

3
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:11,600
The first thing I do when I get up is going to the cozy little washroom.
起床后，我做的第一件事就是去那间温馨的小洗手间。

4
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:18,880
And my favorite thing about this room is the little cute window that just pops right open.
而这间屋子里我最喜欢的，就是那扇轻轻一推就打开的可爱小窗。

5
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:26,990
So I can start my morning brushing my teeth while looking outside at nature and listening to the beautiful bird sounds.
这样，早晨刷牙的时候，我可以一边看窗外的自然风景，一边听悦耳的鸟鸣。

6
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:32,800
It's funny, you never really think about how, first thing when you get up to brush your teeth, you're staring at a mirror.
挺有意思的，你平时不会特意想到：起床刷牙时，第一眼盯着的就是镜子。

7
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:39,119
It's nice to just wake up and look outside and not be focused on your own image.
醒来就看看窗外，而不用把注意力放在自己的样子上，这种感觉很好。

8
00:00:39,119 --> 00:00:42,479
My skincare routine these mornings have been ultra simple.
最近这些早晨，我的护肤步骤都特别简单。

9
00:00:42,479 --> 00:00:48,320
I usually just don't do anything, or the most I'll do is splash my face with some cold water.
我通常什么也不做，最多就是往脸上拍点冷水。

10
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:54,079
I haven't really been using much of any product, and my skin's just been feeling very balanced.
最近我没怎么用护肤品，皮肤的状态倒一直很稳定。

11
00:00:54,079 --> 00:00:59,519
So it's been interesting seeing the simplification of my life in all areas.
所以，看着生活的各个方面都慢慢变得简单，我觉得挺有意思。

12
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:06,079
After brushing up, I use one of the little cushions or a blanket to put on the floor.
洗漱后，我拿一个小坐垫，或者一条毯子，铺在地板上。

13
00:01:06,079 --> 00:01:10,079
And I start my morning Vipassana meditation.
然后，我开始早上的内观冥想。

14
00:01:10,079 --> 00:01:14,879
I've been really good at maintaining an hour every morning, so I'm very proud of myself.
最近我每天早上都能坚持一个小时，所以我为自己感到很骄傲。

15
00:01:14,879 --> 00:01:26,160
I've been using Insight Timer to give me a nice little starting and ending gong sound instead of a beep-beep alarm clock, and I love it.
我一直用 Insight Timer，让轻轻的锣声提示开始和结束，代替闹钟的哔哔声，我很喜欢。

16
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:32,720
Prior to doing this 10-day meditation course, I could not even maintain meditating five minutes a day.
参加这次十天的冥想课程之前，我甚至没法坚持每天冥想五分钟。

17
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:38,640
And then, coming out of it, I can just sit and meditate for a whole hour every morning, like a piece of cake.
但结束课程后，我每天早上都能坐下来冥想整整一个小时，轻松得很。

18
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:42,660
Still blows my mind when I think about it.
现在想起来，我还是觉得很不可思议。

19
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:50,800
I love starting my day with a warm cup of tea, just to give the belly a big old hug.
我喜欢用一杯温热的茶开启一天，就像给肚子一个大大的拥抱。

20
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:52,880
I'm having a mint tea today.
我今天喝的是薄荷茶。

21
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:55,921
There are so many different types of mint here.
这里有好多不同种类的薄荷。

22
00:01:55,921 --> 00:01:59,121
I didn't even realize that there were so many mint species.
我以前都没意识到，薄荷竟然有这么多种。

23
00:01:59,121 --> 00:02:03,601
The one that I will be using today is the chocolate mint.
我今天要用的是巧克力薄荷。

24
00:02:03,601 --> 00:02:10,001
And it just has this really sharp freshness to it, kind of like a spearmint.
它有一种很鲜明、清爽的气息，有点像留兰香薄荷。

25
00:02:10,001 --> 00:02:11,121
So delicious.
真好喝。

26
00:02:11,121 --> 00:02:15,441
I'm gonna mix it with some dandelion honey that Heidi's made.
我准备加一点 Heidi 做的蒲公英蜂蜜，把它们混合起来。

27
00:02:15,441 --> 00:02:19,961
And the combo is just absolutely delectable.
这个搭配实在是太美味了。

28
00:02:26,241 --> 00:02:38,401
These days, I've also started carving out time in the morning to practice music because living with a family where everyone loves to sing and plays an instrument has really reignited my appreciation for music.
最近我也开始在早晨特意腾出时间练习音乐。和一个人人都爱唱歌、会演奏乐器的家庭一起生活，让我重新找回了对音乐的喜爱。

29
00:02:38,401 --> 00:02:43,921
I used to take piano lessons as a kid, but it felt way more like a chore than enjoyment.
我小时候学过钢琴，但当时它更像一项不得不完成的任务，而不是享受。

30
00:02:43,921 --> 00:02:51,561
But now, before everyone wakes up, I’ve been really loving spending some time on the bench playing old songs and learning new ones.
但现在，趁大家还没起床，我很享受坐在琴凳上，弹弹旧曲子，再学几首新曲子。

31
00:02:51,561 --> 00:02:57,161
After having breakfast and those hours of pure enjoyment, I hop into work.
吃完早餐，享受过这几个小时的闲适时光后，我就投入工作。

32
00:02:57,161 --> 00:03:03,721
I turn off airplane mode, turn my signal back on so I can check any messages I have for the day.
我关掉飞行模式，重新打开网络信号，这样就能看看今天收到的消息。

33
00:03:03,721 --> 00:03:13,071
I also really like changing work locations as I'm changing the type of task, just to keep things interesting.
我也很喜欢随着任务类型的变化换一换工作地点，让事情保持一点新鲜感。

34
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:24,040
When your body starts to get tired or your brain gets frustrated, remember to also take a break.
当身体开始疲惫，或者脑子有点烦躁时，记得也让自己休息一下。

35
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:27,241
And no, scrolling on your phone does not count.
还有，刷手机可不算哦。

36
00:03:27,241 --> 00:03:34,920
Go outside, just stare at the sky, or find a weird exercise that you can do.
到外面去，看看天空，或者找个有点奇怪、自己能做的运动。

37
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:36,751
I have no idea how people do these.
我真不知道别人是怎么做到这些动作的。

38
00:03:48,681 --> 00:03:54,661
And if you're hungry, why not go forage for a little snack?
如果饿了，何不去找点野外的小零食呢？

39
00:03:58,681 --> 00:04:00,121
So sweet.
好甜。

40
00:04:00,121 --> 00:04:08,040
And on mornings where I'm doing work that I don't need any Wi-Fi, I'll come to the little fold-down table in the shepherd's hut.
在那些做不需要网络的工作的早晨，我会来到牧羊人小屋里的那张小折叠桌前。

41
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:13,961
And it's actually super great way to stay very focused when I'm doing editing or work like that.
做剪辑或类似工作时，这真是一个能让自己保持专注的好办法。

42
00:04:13,961 --> 00:04:21,801
I'll probably just replicate that in the future by turning off my Wi-Fi signal if I really need to be in the zone.
以后，如果真的需要进入专注状态，我可能会通过关掉网络信号来重现这种感觉。

43
00:04:21,801 --> 00:04:28,441
But also remember that, as wonderful as routines are, we shouldn't get too attached to them.
不过也要记住：习惯再好，我们也不该过分依赖它们。

44
00:04:28,441 --> 00:04:31,001
Our lives are constantly changing.
我们的生活一直都在变化。

45
00:04:31,001 --> 00:04:38,040
So be flexible, be open, be willing to say yes to a spontaneous morning swim.
所以，灵活一点，敞开一点，也愿意接受一次说来就来的晨泳。

46
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:43,321
And always listen to your body, to your heart, what feels right.
也要一直听听身体和内心的感受，留意什么让自己觉得合适。

47
00:04:43,321 --> 00:04:45,561
And be like water.
像水一样，顺势而行。
